    "body": "Maybe this was added later, but my status config looks like this: \r\n```toml\r\n[status]\r\ndisabled = false\r\nformat = \"[$symbol$common_meaning$signal_name$maybe_int]($style)\"\r\npipestatus_format = \"\\\\[$pipestatus\\\\]=>[$symbol$common_meaning$signal_name$maybe_int]($style)\"\r\npipestatus = true\r\nmap_symbol = true\r\nstyle = \"bold #0000ff\"\r\nsymbol = \"[](bold #ff0000)\"\r\nrecognize_signal_code = true\r\nsuccess_symbol = \"[✓](#00ff00)\"\r\nsignal_symbol = \"[](#ffff00)\"\r\n```\r\nand my prompt for a pipe situation looks like this:\r\n\r\n```\r\n(ins)❯ echo \"what\" | yes | cat | head -n 1 | ls dne | cat\r\n\"dne\": No such file or directory (os error 2)\r\n\r\n2021-10-16 05:14:01 ubuntu@spike:~ 21ms [✓|PIPE|PIPE|PIPE|USAGE|✓]=>✓\r\n(ins)❯ echo \"what\" | cat | cat > /dev/null\r\n\r\n2021-10-16 05:14:30 ubuntu@spike:~ 10ms [✓|✓|✓]=>✓\r\n(ins)❯\r\n```\r\n\r\nEDIT: This is with bash ... I have had some trouble with fish not displaying pipestatus, but i could just be fishing wrong as I don't know it as well as bash yet.",
